      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ui): detect session pull requests and pin status chips above the chat composer",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen an agent session does work on a branch and opens a pull request, the Control UI chat view gives no indication that the PR exists, whether CI is green, or whether it already merged. Operators have to leave the chat and hunt through GitHub to answer \"did that work land?\" — exactly the status that should be visible where the conversation happens.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Gateway now detects pull requests for the session's working branch and the chat view pins status chips directly above the composer, one per PR: number, repo, branch, `+adds −dels`, a CI check rollup dot, and draft/merged/closed state, each linking to the PR.\n\n- New `controlUi.sessionPullRequests` RPC (`operator.read`, appended descriptor) resolves the session's checkout (worktree/spawned cwd, falling back to the agent workspace), reads branch + `origin` remote via git, and queries the GitHub API for PRs whose head is that branch (`src/gateway/control-ui-session-prs.ts`). Fork checkouts fall back to the parent repo; the remote default branch is skipped so plain sessions spend no GitHub quota.\n- The existing SSRF-hardened link-preview adapter was split into a shared `src/gateway/control-ui-github-api.ts` (pinned origin, manual redirects, bounded bodies, `GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN`) reused by both surfaces; no new config surface.\n- Rate limits degrade instead of erroring: results are cached per branch (60s success / 5min while limited), and a quota-exhausted refresh serves the last-known chips flagged `rateLimited`, which the UI renders as a warning icon with the tooltip \"GitHub API rate limit reached. Pull request status may be out of date until the limit resets.\" A bare GitHub 403 (permission response) is deliberately not treated as a rate limit; optional diff/check sub-fetches degrade to a chip without those fields.\n- The chip row (`ui/src/pages/chat/components/chat-pull-requests.ts`) refreshes on session switch, on connect, and on a 60s timer; dismissing a chip (X) hides it per session in the browser profile (localStorage). Merged/closed PRs skip diff/CI fetches and render state only.\n\n## User Impact\n\nChat sessions whose checkout sits on a non-default GitHub branch now show live PR chips above the composer — including CI state and merge status — without leaving the conversation. Sessions with no PR, non-GitHub remotes, or default-branch checkouts see no change. When GitHub's API quota is exhausted (common without a `GH_TOKEN`), chips stay visible with a stale-data warning instead of disappearing.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRendered chips (mock-gateway e2e fixture, light theme — open PR with passing CI and rate-limit warning, merged PR below):\n\n![session PR chips above the composer](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/session-pr-chips/chips-light.png)\n\nLive GitHub API verification (real api.github.com, no mocks): branch `claude/browser-tabs-tighter-header` detects merged PR #103469; branch `codex/fix-macos-old-dashboard-chrome` detects draft PR #103524 with `+25 −9`, `checks: \"failing\"`, and checks URL; a branch with no PR returns an empty chip list.\n\nTests and gates:\n- `pnpm test src/gateway/control-ui-session-prs.test.ts src/gateway/server-methods/control-ui.test.ts src/gateway/server-methods-list.test.ts src/gateway/control-ui-github-preview.test.ts` — 114 passed (remote-URL parsing, state derivation, checks rollup, fork fallback, rate-limit staleness, permission-403 degradation, handler validation).\n- `pnpm test ui/src/pages/chat/components/chat-pull-requests.test.ts` — 8 passed (chip rendering, merged/rate-limit rules, dismissal storage bounds).\n- `pnpm test ui/src/e2e/chat-pull-requests.e2e.test.ts` — real-browser proof that chips render above the composer, the warning shows on non-terminal chips only, and dismissal works.\n- `pnpm check:changed` — exit 0 (run locally with `OPENCLAW_CHECK_CHANGED_REMOTE_CHILD=1` because Blacksmith Testbox leases repeatedly shut down mid-hydration during this session; two delegated attempts died at \"Setup Node environment\").\n- `pnpm ui:i18n:sync` + `ui:i18n:check` clean (new `chat.pullRequests.*` strings, raw-copy fallbacks).\n- Structured Codex review (gpt-5.5) on the branch diff, iterated until clean; its three findings (permission 403s misclassified as rate limits, missing scoped-agent context on the new RPC, and stale check conclusions rolling up as passing) were each fixed with regression tests.\n",
